//! The exact paths of the generated predicates in the width-aware limb variant: each step in `i64`
//! when its certificate fits 63 bits, otherwise in a `Wide32` of as many 32-bit limbs as its
//! operands' certified bits need, so every limb product is one 32 × 32 → 64-bit multiply, native on
//! WebAssembly, and operands of different widths multiply without being widened first (chapter 23.3
//! of the kernel architecture, `projects/engines/geometry/architecture/23-performance.md`; piece
//! G42). For each predicate, `<predicate>_value` performs the steps of the predicate module's
//! `value`, in their order and with their names, each held in the type above, so it returns the
//! same value, converted back to the shipped path's type. The benchmarks compare the two on every
//! target, and the tests check that they agree on every input they draw and at the grid's extremes.
//!
//! Guarantees: as each predicate module's `value`. Every step is a checked method, the certificate
//! in the predicate module's header bounds every step within the type it is held in here (a type at
